      "attempt_id": "A_direct_attempt_2",
      "message": "lly.\n- `can_transition(old, new)` returning `(old, new) in _ALLOWED_TRANSITIONS` \u2014 v2 semantics reproduced without importing `semkg_contract`.\n\n## Local check (run against the written file, not the contract)\n```\nversion 2\n('paid','refunded')  -> True\n('new','paid')       -> True\n('new','cancelled')  -> True\n('paid','paid')      -> False\n('refunded','paid')  -> False\n('cancelled','paid') -> False\n```\nSo `can_transition('paid', 'refunded')` is **True** under the v2 contract, and the producer matches it on all sampled pairs. No imports of `semkg_contract`, no changes outside the attempt directory, and no repository-wide tests were run.\n\nOne note worth flagging: because the contract was at version 2 when I read it, the \"v2 behavior\" is simply the one set above \u2014 there was no separate v1/v2 divergence to reconcile. If the intent was that v2 *changed* the `('paid','refunded')` outcome (e.g. from True to False), that change is not present in the contract I was given, so my copy reflects True."
